From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000008 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Keystone P550 Integration <keystone-p550@example.invalid>
Date: Sat, 22 Aug 2026 00:00:00 +0800
Subject: [PATCH] sm: permit rdcycle only in the enclave context

The P550 Ubuntu kernel clears scounteren.CY, so copying the host value into a
new enclave makes Keystone's unmodified test-fib-bench trap forever on its
first rdcycle. Give the enclave context access to the architectural cycle
counter expected by the official example. The normal context swap restores
Linux's original scounteren value when returning to the host.

This changes only the separately saved enclave S-mode CSR state; it does not
enable rdcycle for Ubuntu userspace. mcounteren.CY is already enabled by
OpenSBI during hart initialization.

Upstream-Status: Inappropriate [P550 Linux counter-access policy]
---
 src/thread.c | 7 +++++--
 1 file changed, 5 insertions(+), 2 deletions(-)

diff --git a/src/thread.c b/src/thread.c
index a13ad82..a45ceab 100644
--- a/src/thread.c
+++ b/src/thread.c
@@ -107,8 +107,11 @@ void clean_smode_csrs(struct thread_state* state){
 
   state->prev_csrs.sie = 0;
   state->prev_csrs.stvec = 0;
-  // For now we take whatever the OS was doing
-  state->prev_csrs.scounteren = csr_read(scounteren);
+  /*
+   * The official fib-bench enclave reads cycle from U-mode. Linux keeps
+   * host U-mode counter access disabled, so grant CY only to the enclave.
+   */
+  state->prev_csrs.scounteren = 1UL;
   state->prev_csrs.sscratch = 0;
   state->prev_csrs.sepc = 0;
   state->prev_csrs.scause = 0;
-- 
